{
  "id": "Compound::DB00595 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Oxytetracycline, a tetracycline antibiotic, is implicated in the transport of organic anions through the cell membrane, as evidenced by its interaction with Slc22a7, which is involved in organic anion transport. This relationship is supported by the shared pathway through the Slc22a11 gene, which is part of the organic anion transport system. The evidence from the three paths collectively suggests that Oxytetracycline may influence Slc22a11 through its interaction with Slc22a7, which in turn affects the transport of organic anions. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of a common ancestor in the Tetracyclines group further supports the notion of a shared biological function, reinforcing the hypothesis that Oxytetracycline may modulate Slc22a11 through a pathway involving organic anion transport.",
